item.description:
&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I am overwhelmed by finding you folks at this moment, exactly what I was asking for. A beautiful stranger on the other side of the world, in a &quot;random&quot; gene keys community cauldron call, lead me to Hospicing Modernity in response to my desire to move deep sadness and layers of ancestral settler guilt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thank you for this essential and pertinent collaborative and creative work. The simultaneous invitation to look hard into the deeply layered collective malaise, the crevices created through centuries of our settler privilege,  while holding space for coming together in new ways. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I am an aging straight white settler born in what was known to us as Montreal.  I climbed the mountain of privilege in what is known to us as downtown Vancouver and now live, re-settled as co-custodian on stolen land in the colonized indigenous town of Axixic Central Mexico. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our collaborative creative community, la cochera cultural, is intended to live in after us, &quot;gifted&quot; back to the community in perpetuity. We host an annual Festival Michi-cihualli to honor the goddess of this lake and these precious lands. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This work of yours has inspired me to find ways with our team,  to deepen to impact of this festival bringing more of our town&#039;s indigenous peoples together with white settlers, national and international and setting ways to move forward each day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;witn deep gratitude, I am anxious to look deeper into your wealth of resources for this decolonizing work we are being called to do. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Jennifer Faith Stanley&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;co-founder/co-temporary custodian&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are doing good work. You are blessed. The world is flourishing because of you. The gods are happy. Gratitude to you Vanessa.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

In reply to &lt;a href=&quot;https://decolonialfutures.net/2023/06/23/prayer-songs/comment-page-1/#comment-5607&quot;&gt;Mikie Feighan&lt;/a&gt;.

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Irish language can hold that grief, that pain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It knows it well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bringing it to healing waters in Ireland &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sounds like an act of radical&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tenderness&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Truly my heart has been stretched and broken over and over again with my own experiences within the health care system, the discomfort and deceptive and contradictory ways in which this system operates has been infuriating. Many caucasians have said to me the system is really a game that you need to know how to play and thats right, thats been my experience and I do not play the game well because I had the assumption that these people wanted to help me but in reality theyre just showing up for a job that is focused around money and resources that are supposed to be available to help us. They&#039;re SUPPOSED to but that doesn&#039;t mean they really want to help us, that is a big mental shift I have had to make, one that makes the rejection and long waits a little bit less heartbreaking and a little more empowering. Any time I&#039;ve mentioned holistic healing including nutritional changes I&#039;ve been refused care &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These words are a collective response to the poem by members of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://sites.google.com/view/nubianbookclub/summer-2024&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow ugc&quot;&gt;Nubian Book Club in July, 2024.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Allyship is not transactional or extractive&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is relational, fluid, contextual, ever-changing, shape-shifting&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is convergence and heart work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It invites the real -&#160; real hurt, real harm, real opportunities for healing and hoping through community&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It acknowledges that we are all teachers and we are all learners&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It requires the deepest interrogation of ourselves and each other&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It necessitates the destruction of the ego.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Can you let go of your ego?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is a way of life, moment by moment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who determines who can claim and who is claimed as an ally?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What or whose definition of allyship do we use?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Is it a verb, a noun, an adjective?&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are they simply weapons of mass construction?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Can you be an ally to your own community?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Is there one way to be an ally given the diversity in our intersectional identities, politics, and experiences?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Does it always involve risk?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And when I do take the risk, does it matter who&#039;s watching?&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Does my risk speak to what&#039;s needed now?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Being an ally is continuously questioning what it means to be an ally&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Risking, acting, questioning, undoing, unlearning, striving, and calling in, for love and liberation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I step up without conditions or expectations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beautifully written wisdom of the ages - thank you for sharing this beautiful story&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mentoring comes to my mind, being mature means for me to be a wise mentor for the younger. I am grateful for the work of Jon Young and Bill Plotkin and their teachers, mentors and elders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Good stuff. Be kind to yourself while trying.  &lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Steve G&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;

&lt;!-- wp:paragraph --&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I appreciate the dichotomy in the list outlined.  It is an example of the complexity and heaviness of getting to know me all over again. There is no time to rest in my knowing but to lay bare my being.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;!-- /wp:paragraph --&gt;
